Bayroq tongi — credits for third-party material

Code: cel.js, post.js, fx.js and head80.js (adapted: a schoolboy with short hair, a black suit and a white shirt),
and the instrument synthesis in music/score.py, are from the Lemo-Opuscar library's cel-anime-80s demo
(https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Lemomo (LemoLab).
The story, shots, backgrounds, figure, flag, harmony, melodies and arrangement are new for this film.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, texts in fonts/): Kanit (Cadson Demak), Barlow Semi Condensed (Jeremy Tribby).

Music and sound: synthesised in code (numpy), no samples, no recordings. The score is original; it does not quote the state anthem.
Flag: the standard 1:2 construction of the State Flag of the Republic of Uzbekistan, redrawn as paths in flag.js.
Facts: gov.uz (State symbols), lex.uz (Law of 18.11.1991 No. 407-XII).
Diyorbek does not speak: captions and a name card carry the words.
